# HISTORICAL / SUPERSEDED / NONEXECUTABLE

## Retired OpenCode configuration guide

**Status: QUARANTINED. Do not follow, install, launch, or restore the setup that
was previously documented here.**

This path is retained only so old links resolve to an explicit retirement
notice. The former document was an operational guide for a superseded external
model-provider control plane. Its provider routing, credentials, plugins,
commands, agents, caches, launchers, and configuration examples are not active
repository instructions and carry no execution or scientific authority.

Current authority is:

1. [`AGENTS.md`](../AGENTS.md) for provider, delegation, safety, and acceptance
   boundaries.
2. [`QUICKSTART.md`](QUICKSTART.md) for the supported OpenAI backend and
   Codex-native development workflow.
3. [`.codex/cost-cache-policy.md`](../.codex/cost-cache-policy.md) for local-first
   context, cost, and verification policy.

Historical files elsewhere in the repository remain evidence only. They must
not be used to reactivate another model provider or to override the current
OpenAI ChatGPT/Codex-native policy.
